.TH PROSHIM 1 "September 19, 2026" maux
.SH NAME
proshim \- host a compatible ProDOS SYSTEM program
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B proshim
.I file.system
.SH DESCRIPTION
Load a compatible ProDOS 8 SYSTEM program at $2000 in a process bank.
A shim supplies supported ProDOS MLI calls and monitor entry points,
and connects the program's console I/O to maux.
.PP
The tenant takes over the process. It runs cooperatively, yielding at
translated MLI calls; a compute loop need not yield to other work.
Only programs tested against the supported shim surface should be run.
.PP
This is a compatibility-development tool, supplied on its dedicated
image. It is not a general Apple II emulator or a promise that any
SYSTEM program will work.
.SH FILES
/usr/man/PROSHIM  this page
.SH "SEE ALSO"
bpatch(1), plasma(1)
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Startup, usage, open/read and size failures return 1. A successfully loaded tenant determines how the session terminates.
.SH BUGS
Programs that depend on unsupported hardware, ProDOS internals, interrupt behaviour or ROM entry points may fail or hang. Preserve originals and test patched tenants on disposable images.
